Z||000000||kornholio||10-21-2000||01:00 AM||||I tried to jump start my friend's car with my Fiero today and there wasn't enough power to get it started.  So we get another vehicle and it starts up right away.  I know for a fact that my alternator charges at 14.3 volts at idle because I checked it with a volt meter.  Is there something wrong or is my alternator just made to run my vehicle only?||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||10-21-2000||01:29 AM||||It's not all about volts. Your car might not have had enough AMPS to do the job<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-21-2000||06:16 AM||||It could be a bad batt.? How many cranking amps it the batt on there now? I have that problem with a couple cars. You have to hook the jumper cables up and start your car and either rev it or let it idle for a few minuts to charge the other batt, then it starts fine.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-21-2000||05:36 PM||||could also be the jumper cables. you might not have had a good bite on the Fiero or you could have bad cables. Just because they look good doesn't mean they are. ||||reg||1
